  "question": {
    "text": "The extremities of a diagonal of a rectangle are <math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>0,0</mn></mrow></mfenced></math> and <math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>4,3</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>.</mo></math> The equations of the tangents to the circumcircle of the rectangle which are parallel to the diagonal are"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>&#177;</mo><mn>5</mn></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math><mn>3</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>±</mo><mn>10</mn></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math><mn>3</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>±</mo><mn>25</mn></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>6</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>8</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>&#177;</mo><mn>25</mn></math>",
      "is_correct": true
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "D"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "Let,&nbsp;<math><mi>A</mi><mi>B</mi><mi>C</mi><mi>D</mi></math> be the rectangle such that the coordinates of the vertices <math><mi>A</mi></math> and <math><mi>C</mi></math> of diagonal <math><mi>A</mi><mi>C</mi></math> are <math><mi>A</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>0,0</mn></mrow></mfenced></math> and <math><mi>C</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>4,3</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>.</mo></math><br /><img src=\"assets\\st0032_37ab404b46f9.png\" style=\"width: 220px; height: 173px;\" /><br />The equation of the circumcircle of rectangle <math><mi>A</mi><mi>B</mi><mi>C</mi><mi>D</mi></math> is<br /><math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mfenced><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mfenced><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math><br /><math><mo>&#8658;</mo><msup><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mi>y</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math> &hellip; <math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced></math><br />The equation of a line parallel to <math><mi>A</mi><mi>C</mi></math> is<br /><math><mn>3</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>&#955;</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math> &hellip; <math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfenced></math><br />If it touches the circle <math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>,</mo></math> then<br /><math><mfenced close=\"|\" open=\"|\" separators=\"|\"><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>&#955;</mi></mrow><mrow><msqrt><mn>9</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>16</mn></msqrt></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mn>4</mn><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>9</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn></mrow></mfrac></msqrt></math><br /><math><mo>&#8658;</mo><mfenced close=\"|\" open=\"|\" separators=\"|\"><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>&#955;</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>5</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>5</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac></math><br /><math><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>&#955;</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>&#177;</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>25</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac></math><br />Substituting the value of <math><mi>&#955;</mi></math> in <math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>,</mo></math> we obtain that the equations of the required tangents are<br /><math><mn>3</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>&#177;</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>25</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math>"
  }
